# Frontend

- Use Next.js App Router, React, strict TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui primitives, and `output: "standalone"`.
- Application base path is `/app`; use centralized URL/API helpers and never scatter hardcoded `/app`.
- Server Components are default. Add `"use client"` only for interaction, browser APIs, or client state.
- Browser API base is `/app/api/v1`; SSR uses the internal backend URL.
- Prefer URL/search params for shareable state and local component state for transient UI; add Zustand only for genuinely shared client state.
- Validate forms with shared schemas; server validation remains authoritative.
- Russian is the default UI language. Keep user copy clear, formal, and action-oriented; avoid exposing provider/CUDA/internal errors.
- Every async action has loading, empty, success, retryable error, terminal error, and permission-denied states.
- Streaming chat must support cancel, reconnect/error display, source citations, model limitations, and partial-response safety.
- Approval screens show exact proposed action, target, data diff, risk, model/agent version, and approve/reject controls.
- Never render raw model HTML. Sanitize Markdown, links, filenames, previews, and downloaded content.
- Do not store access tokens, secrets, document bodies, or privileged approval payloads in `localStorage`.
- Enforce accessible labels, keyboard flow, focus management, contrast, reduced motion, and responsive layouts.
- UI permission checks improve UX only; never assume they enforce authorization.
- Keep feature components colocated; reusable primitives stay domain-neutral.
